@@ -1,3 +1,18 @@
+pve-cluster (9.1.7+supermox4) trixie; urgency=medium
+
+  * init.d/pve-cluster: stop, status and restart find pmxcfs by its executable,
+    so a missing or stale pidfile no longer makes stop do nothing and restart
+    start a second pmxcfs on the same mount (which hung every read of /etc/pve
+    and made PVE's own cluster join abort).
+  * init.d/pve-cluster: seeding /etc/pve/storage.cfg retries for up to 30
+    seconds. pmxcfs mounts /etc/pve read-only until corosync reports quorum,
+    a few seconds after corosync starts, so on the live ISO the first write
+    failed with "Permission denied" on every boot.
+  * debian: the postinst no longer writes corosync.conf inside a build chroot
+    (the build-chroot test was inverted in +supermox3).
+
+ -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 18:40:00 -0800
